# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data. None of this belongs in version control -- the working tree is
# ~27 GB, dominated by source video and derived frames.
#
# Everything under data/ is either an input you already hold, or is
# reproducible from those inputs with the commands in README.md.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
_archive/

# Source video anywhere
*.avi
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv

# Derived per-frame artefacts
frames_*/
out_*/
*.npz

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Results.
# Commented out deliberately: the CSVs are a few MB and are the actual
# findings, so you may WANT them tracked for the write-up. Uncomment to
# exclude them.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# *.csv

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
.Python
env/
venv/
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
live_view_frame_*.png
*.log
.Rhistory

# A running Streamlit server holds src/review/app.py open and can drop a stale
# copy back at the repo root. The real file lives in src/review/.
/app.py

# Word/Excel lock files, created while a document is open
~$*

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Report artefacts.
# The manuscript itself is deliberately NOT tracked. This repository is
# public, and text published here before submission can be matched by
# similarity checking against its own online copy.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Report_*.docx
Report_*.pdf
~$Report*
.~lock.*#
*.tmp

# Intermediate files from extracting revised prose out of the manuscript
figures/his_*.json
figures/_preview/

# The manuscript prose and the script that assembles it. Kept out of the
# repository for the same reason as the .docx: published text can be matched
# against its own online copy by similarity checking. figures/make_figures.py
# stays tracked, since it generates the figures from the pipeline outputs and
# is part of the analysis rather than the write-up.
figures/report_text.py
figures/report_text_rest.py
figures/build_report.py

# Vector copies of the figures. The 300 dpi PNGs are what the report uses and
# both are regenerated by figures/make_figures.py.
figures/output/*.pdf
